   "review_rating": 5,
   "review_text": "We went the Saturday before Easter for a family meal. The building and architecture is fantastic. It feels similar to large modern cabins or houses  out in Big Sky. Large fire places, rough wood floors, stone oven, large wall of wine, long family style tables, and the smell of chicken on the fire rotisserie breathe life into this place well before the food arrives. Our waitress was very attentive and managed a group of 5 adults and 4 children with ease. The food I had was good, although portioned at what is probably a healthier size than I prefer! I had the duck gnocchi, but wish I would have also had an appetizer. Next time I will. There are some items that priced as high end dishes, but there are options that are priced more accommodating. My wife had a salad and said it was alright.",
